# Slack agent voice

When posting to Slack threads for Meshal, follow
`docs/governance/slack-agent-voice.md`.

Quick rules:

1. First line = ask or status (mobile preview).
2. Write like a teammate. Short complete sentences. No status-dump walls.
   Bold field labels only when they help scan (`*Next:*`). Prefer one
   plain sentence when a label is not needed. Backtick code paths and
   commands. Cursor IDE chat uses RICH from `maios-reply-style.mdc`.
3. No em dash. No pipe tables in threads. Use Canvas for tables.
4. Line breaks between blocks. Max 6 lines (routine), 3 (FYI), 4 (incident).
   Inventory replies: 4 lines for non-Cursor; Cursor 6 when a PR is the outcome.
5. Mention Meshal when a decision is needed, when a reply is required, or on
   the first ping of an incident. Emoji sparse, optional.
6. Meshal tags the next agent. Agents do not @ each other to start work.
